{
  "requirement": "Saving encodes the completed result using its Serde JSON representation and\npreserves the dependencies captured in `Fingerprinted`.\n`Record`, `Dependency`, and `Fingerprint` support\nSerde when their type parameters do. The graph's node\nidentities and edge labels need not implement Serde unless its storage backend\nrequires those bounds.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Record<N, L = ()> {\n    pub version: Option<CriterionVersion>,\n    pub dependencies: Vec<Dependency<N, L>>,\n    pub output: Value,\n}\n\nimpl<N, L> Record<N, L> {\n    pub fn new(\n        version: Option<CriterionVersion>,\n        dependencies: Vec<Dependency<N, L>>,\n        output: Value,\n    ) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<N: Clone, L: Clone> Clone for Record<N, L>;\nimpl<N: Debug, L: Debug> Debug for Record<N, L>;\nimpl<'de, N, L> Deserialize<'de> for Record<N, L> where N: Deserialize<'de>, L: Deserialize<'de>;\nimpl<N, L> Serialize for Record<N, L> where N: Serialize, L: Serialize;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. Saving encodes the completed result as Serde JSON.\n2. Saving preserves the dependencies captured in `Fingerprinted`.\n3. `Record`, `Dependency` and `Fingerprint` support Serde when their type parameters do.\n4. `Record` has the shape `{version, dependencies, output}` and a `Record::new` constructor.\n5. `Record` implements Clone, Debug, Serialize and Deserialize.\n6. Node identities and edge labels need not implement Serde. This states no obligation to test.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Encoding of the output.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` stores the results of `verify`. It asserts the stored `Record.output` is `json!({\"satisfied\":false,\"details\":[\"missing edge case\"]})` for a struct answer and `json!(null)` for a unit answer. It also asserts the loaded output equals the original typed answer, and that `Record` dependencies are empty when none were captured.\n- **Dependency preservation.** `contracts.rs#fn[input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations]` reads node 2 during execution and persists the result. It asserts the stored record's dependencies are exactly `[Dependency::Node(Node(2), Fingerprint::new(\"text-v1\", \"after\"))]`. That checks the `Fingerprinted` dependencies reach the saved `Record` with the right fingerprint.\n- **Serde round-trip and type parameters.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs#fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]` round-trips records through `FileEvidenceStorage`.\n  - It builds the record with `Record::new`, which exercises the constructor.\n  - It checks that version, dependencies and output survive. The `record` helper supplies a `Dependency::Node` and a `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`, each with a `Fingerprint`.\n  - It round-trips a `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` with a `String` label and a non-ASCII value, and compares dependencies for equality.\n  - It checks that loading with an incompatible node type or label type (`u8`) gives a JSON error.\n- **Serde with generic parameters.** The same test uses `String` nodes with `()` and `String` labels, which shows the Serde support depends on the type parameters.\n- **Opaque types.** `public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the published exports against the appendix. Opaque node and label types are accepted in the unmarked `domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors`. The text only says Serde \"need not\" be implemented for them, so this is not an obligation.\n- **Clone and Debug.** Nothing in the marked tests asserts these directly. They are derived trait impls with no conditional or transformation of their own, so the untested-obligation exemption for pass-through code applies. The `Debug` and `Clone` bounds are also exercised at compile time by tests that use `Record`.\n\n**Minor observations, not gaps**\n- The version-encoding test `record_preserves_the_stored_version_encoding` and the serialization-failure tests are relevant but lack a `{test}` reference to this requirement. That is a marking matter, not an adequacy gap.\n- The marked tests round-trip only `Some` versions. The text names no `None` boundary for this requirement.\n\nNo acknowledgments apply.",
